# The images need three files from this repository, and one is each Dockerfile.
# An allowlist keeps the build context tiny and makes it structurally impossible
# for a credential, a session transcript or any other future file to reach an
# image layer.
*
!docker-entrypoint.sh
# Dockerfile.supermemory is named by `build.dockerfile` in docker-compose.yml, so
# it has to be in the context like any other build input. Without this line the
# supermemory build fails on a missing Dockerfile. Nothing else from the
# repository reaches that image -- it fetches its binary from the release.
!Dockerfile.supermemory
# The parent has to be un-excluded as well: a file below a directory that `*`
# matched stays out of the context otherwise.
!scripts/
!scripts/prune-platform-packages.js
